The first level contained four fountains, a sink and an altar. A few 
dips later and I've got GDSM. I ignored the bow mostly, collecting 
daggers to throw. With good armor and lots of daggers I cleared much of 
the Mines and went to Sokoban, where I got a bag of holding.

Level 11 contained a bones pile, with a stack of potions, scrolls and 
wands, plus a luckstone, unicorn horn and "oR. I dragged it all back to 
Minetown where I ID'd my stuff and enchanted my (27) daggers to +6. At a 
neutral temple, sac'd some monsters and got Mjollnir. Went through the 
Dungeons, killed some monsters, reached level 12, quaffed a b!oGL, 
killed more monsters, reached level 14 and went questing.

There was a beartrap on the home level, which meant hanging around for 
hundreds of turns while the hunters got the $#@%! out of the way. Scorpy 
went down to four daggers without even touching me. A centaur had a wand 
of death, which he managed to kill himself with, so I took it.

I continued to the Castle, killed most of the inhabitants, grabbed the 
/oW and got GoP, HoB, MM and !oGA. The throne gave me another wish, so I 
got a T-shirt. (It's not the size of your sword, it's how #enhance'd you 
are with it.) I wrote a pile of magic mapping scrolls, enchanted my 
armor and jumped into the Valley.

At this point I had 80-odd HP and AC:-23. I continued through Gehennom. 
I didn't bother to wait for Asmo and Baal to come back after throwing a 
few daggers at them, but continued down. Juiblex came over for a chat, 
and I killed him before he swallowed me. In Orcus' Town I fell down a 
trap door, came back upstairs, threw a few daggers at Orcus, killed him 
and took his wand. Somewhere around here I replaced my jumping boots 
with speed boots.

Vlad went down to four daggers. Found the VS and went back to Rodney's 
tower. Rodney summoned an arch-lich before eating death ray. The 
arch-lich summoned some more friends, and eventually got disintegrated 
by a black dragon. Did the invocation, moved through the Sanctum without 
much trouble. The high priest was wearing a CoMR, the bastard, so I had 
to chuck more daggers at him. Moloch seemed rather perturbed, judging 
from the lightning bolts that kept bouncing of my "oR. Rodney showed up 
late, so I zapped him. Grabbed the Amulet and quaffed a c!oGL to go back up.

The mysterious force was a minor annoyance. I made it back to the 
Dungeons, grabbed some food on the way up and headed for the planes. 
Rodney put in his obligatory cameo. On Air I used the /oD a couple of 
times to dispatch air elementals (got swallowed once). No problems on 
Fire, wandered around a bit on Water until I found the portal, and made 
it to the Astral Plane.

An arch-lich welcomed me by summoning a few nasties. I dispatched him 
and his friends and went to Door #3 (right). Famine was there, zapped 
him and a few priests. I got surrounded by a few Angels near the temple 
door, and had to use a couple of !oFH. Killed the yellow dragon in the 
doorway and went to the altar. It was chaotic. To Gehennom with it, I 
thought, and pulled a helmet out of my bag. I became chaotic, and 
offered the Amulet to Mars.

